Third-party material used by this project:

- Claude Agent SDK (@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk): used as a dependency under Anthropic's
  terms (see its README). Claude Code is driven with Anthropic or Anthropic-compatible API keys
  only; claude.ai sign-in is never offered (PLAN.md §6).
- catalog/providers.json: model and price data from models.dev (MIT,
  https://github.com/anomalyco/models.dev). Anthropic-compatible endpoints and balance endpoints
  in catalog/curated.json come from cc-switch (MIT, https://github.com/farion1231/cc-switch);
  every entry cites its file and line.
- LiteLLM price cross-check (packages/daemon/src/providers/litellm.ts): prices from BerriAI/litellm's
  model_prices_and_context_window.json (MIT, Copyright (c) 2023 Berri AI,
  https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm). A slice of it (mapped providers' chat prices) is stored in the
  local database to show differences in diagnostics; it never sets a price.
- Geist and Geist Mono fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1), bundled through @fontsource.
- @xyflow/react and @xyflow/system (React Flow), MIT, Copyright (c) 2019-2025 webkid GmbH
  (https://github.com/xyflow/xyflow). The Crew graph hides React Flow's attribution link
  (`proOptions.hideAttribution`), which the MIT licence allows; this notice keeps its copyright.
- packages/ui/src/brand-icons.gen.ts: provider logos from models.dev (MIT,
  https://github.com/anomalyco/models.dev) and the Claude, Google Gemini, Git, GitHub and Ollama
  marks from simple-icons 16.36.0 (CC0-1.0, https://github.com/simple-icons/simple-icons).
  All marks are trademarks of their owners and are used only to name their service.
- Design and architecture ideas from OrchestratorInc/agent-orchestrator and BloopAI/vibe-kanban
  (Apache-2.0), among other projects listed in PRIOR_ART.md. They were read for reference only;
  no code has been copied or ported from them.
- packages/adapter-codex/src/protocol/: TypeScript types generated by `codex app-server generate-ts`
  from openai/codex (Apache-2.0, https://github.com/openai/codex). Generated, not hand-copied; each
  file names the codex version it came from.
